I have to point out this isn't true. There are tons of games where you 
can't actually lose, and tons more where you'll eventually win (because 
of saving, especially autosaving).

Take GTA3, for example. You can't lose, no matter how hard you try. The 
game is fun to play simply *because* it's a game. It's not about winning 
or anything, it's about enjoying yourself. Same for many online games. 
You still have to call them games though.

I agree that the thrill of NetHack (and roguelikes in general) is 
generally from the difficulty. Clearly difficulty is only percieved, 
just look at marvin; you could say every character is ascendable so does 
that make the game pointless?

